{"activity_text": "Anti-Gram+, Anti-MRSA, Anti-inflammatory, Antibiofilm", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "CD", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Peptide design: the peptide was obtained by substituting each phenylalanine with leucine to study the difference between aromatic and aliphatic amino acids in this template. Sequence analysis: APD analysis reveals this sequence is most similar (75%) to BMAP-28 L: 33%; K: 39%; R: 17%. GRAVY: -1.07; M Wt: 2206.859; M formula: C101H196N34O20; Mol ex coeff: 0. Activity: Active against S. aureus MRSA (MIC 16 uM). Also inhibit biofilm formation at MBIC 16 uM and disrupted preformed biofilms at MBEC=8 uM. Similar to LL-37, this variant has more effective anti-inflammatory activity (lower levels ofIL-6, MCP-1, and TNF-alpha) than BMAP-18. In vitro Toxicity: Sheep RBC: no hemolysis till 20 uM. low hemo.lytic (30% at 130 uM) with HC50 >130 uM. Cf.: mellitin caused nearly 100% hemolysis at ~10 uM. HC50 at 16-32 uM to RAW264.7 mouse macrophages. Structure: it became helical after binding to SDS or in 50% TFE. MOA:bacteria: it targets membranes, especially Gram- bacteria.", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "", "hemolytic_activity_text": "", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "37895827", "record_granularity": "entry_text", "reference_text": "Pharmaceuticals (Basel). 2023 Sep 25;16(10):1356. doi: 10.3390/ph16101356. PubMed.", "sequence_key": "APD6:AP03759", "source_id": "AP03759", "source_numeric_id": "03759", "source_path": "APD6/apd6_export/structured/peptides.csv", "source_record_id": "AP03759", "source_table": "peptides.csv", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "", "title": "Multifunctional Properties of BMAP-18 and Its Aliphatic Analog against Drug-Resistant Bacteria.", "unit": "", "﻿database": "APD6"}
